For your background, I would especially prepare:

Inventory Management System → Order → Stock → Reservation → Transaction → Redis → Queue → Database

That can give you a strong real-world project discussion in interviews.

Recommended preparation order

Phase 1 — Must know

NestJS → Modules → Controllers → Services → DI → DTO → Validation → Guards → JWT → TypeORM

Phase 2 — Backend fundamentals

Node.js → Event Loop → Async Programming → HTTP → REST → SQL → Indexing → Transactions

Phase 3 — Production

Redis → Caching → Queues/BullMQ → Rate Limiting → Logging → Error Handling → Docker

Phase 4 — Advanced

Performance → Scalability → Microservices → System Design → AWS


